      "id": "P1",
      "number": 1,
      "text": "From his bag, Eitan took out a wooden stand. There was blue paint on his fingers. He and his father had finished making it late the night before. Suddenly, Noam understood why Eitan had answered so quickly. “I have never felt so embarrassed about assuming the worst,” Noam said. “But I didn't know for sure.” “My first words were unfriendly,” Eitan replied. “I agree. I have learned that explaining things clearly matters.” For a moment, neither boy spoke. Then Noam moved the books, and Eitan placed the stand in the middle. The welcome sign fitted perfectly.",
